														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1702906">
									

<p>Here's a rough analogy:</p>
<p>Imagine our universe is a pool of water in a crater. What we don't know though, is that the crater is at the top of a mountain. As far as we are concerned, the universe is stable and comfortable, but in fact, the only thing keeping our universe from flowing down the mountain is that it can't get over the rim of the crater.</p>
<p>Right? So this guy managed to drill a hole in the side of the crater, and our universe started to leak out. The vacuum bubble inside the machine is the portion of the universe that has already fallen down the mountain. Unfortunately physics works differently at the bottom of the mountain than at the top, so everything that goes into the bubble get destroyed.</p>

							</div>

								
					
